Bar plot for region scores.

positional arguments:
  regions               Region-based file, e.g. BED, GFF, BigWig, ...

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --aspect-ratio ASPECT_RATIO
                        Aspect ratio of this panel. Default is determined by
                        figure type (usually 1.0).
  --title TITLE         Title of this plot.
  --fix-chromosome      Fix chromosome identifier for this plot (add or remove
                        "chr" as required). Use this ifthere is a mismatch
                        between the nomenclature used by different datasets in
                        the figure, specifically if the chromosome prefix for
                        this dataset does not match the plot region
                        definition.
  --hide-x              Hide x-axis for this plot
  --show-minor-ticks    Show minor ticks on genome axis
  --hide-major-ticks    Hide major ticks on genome axis.
  --show-tick-legend    Show tick legend with distance between ticks on genome
                        axis
  -a ATTRIBUTE, --attribute ATTRIBUTE
                        Attribute to plot. Default: score
  -b BIN_SIZE, --bin-size BIN_SIZE
                        Bin size. Specify if you want to bin scores into
                        larger regions (using weighted mean).
  --alpha ALPHA         Transparency of bars. Value between 0 and 1, default:
                        0.5
  -l LABELS [LABELS ...], --labels LABELS [LABELS ...]
                        Labels for region datasets
  -y YLIM YLIM, --ylim YLIM YLIM
                        Y-axis limits.
  -c COLORS [COLORS ...], --colors COLORS [COLORS ...]
                        Colors for region datasets
  --legend-location LEGEND_LOCATION
                        Location of the legend when providing data labels.
usage: fancplot <region> -p <plot type> [-h] [--aspect-ratio ASPECT_RATIO]
                                        [--title TITLE] [--fix-chromosome]
                                        [--hide-x] [--show-minor-ticks]
                                        [--hide-major-ticks]
                                        [--show-tick-legend]
                                        [-g GROUPING_ATTRIBUTE]
                                        [-i INCLUDE [INCLUDE ...]]
                                        [-e EXCLUDE [EXCLUDE ...]] [-S] [-C]
                                        [-w SHADOW_WIDTH] [--no-colors]
                                        features

Layered feature plot.

positional arguments:
  features              Features file (GFF, BED, Tabix).

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --aspect-ratio ASPECT_RATIO
                        Aspect ratio of this panel. Default is determined by
                        figure type (usually 1.0).
  --title TITLE         Title of this plot.
  --fix-chromosome      Fix chromosome identifier for this plot (add or remove
                        "chr" as required). Use this ifthere is a mismatch
                        between the nomenclature used by different datasets in
                        the figure, specifically if the chromosome prefix for
                        this dataset does not match the plot region
                        definition.
  --hide-x              Hide x-axis for this plot
  --show-minor-ticks    Show minor ticks on genome axis
  --hide-major-ticks    Hide major ticks on genome axis.
  --show-tick-legend    Show tick legend with distance between ticks on genome
                        axis
  -g GROUPING_ATTRIBUTE, --grouping GROUPING_ATTRIBUTE
                        GFF attribute to use for grouping into layers. For BED
                        this is always the name column.
  -i INCLUDE [INCLUDE ...], --include INCLUDE [INCLUDE ...]
                        Include only these groups.
  -e EXCLUDE [EXCLUDE ...], --exclude EXCLUDE [EXCLUDE ...]
                        Exclude these groups.
  -S, --no-shadow       Plot element size "as is" without surrounding box to
                        make it more visible.
  -C, --collapse        Plot all elements in one row.
  -w SHADOW_WIDTH, --shadow-width SHADOW_WIDTH
                        Vertical distance between rows of genes in the plot.
  --no-colors           Do not add color to plots.
usage: fancplot <region> -p <plot type> [-h] [--aspect-ratio ASPECT_RATIO]
                                        [--title TITLE] [--fix-chromosome]
                                        [--hide-x] [--show-minor-ticks]
                                        [--hide-major-ticks]
                                        [--show-tick-legend]
                                        [-f FEATURE_TYPES [FEATURE_TYPES ...]]
                                        [-cn COLOR_NEUTRAL]
                                        [-cf COLOR_FORWARD]
                                        [-cr COLOR_REVERSE] [-cs]
                                        [-b BOX_HEIGHT] [-s FONT_SIZE]
                                        [-a ARROW_SIZE] [-l LINE_WIDTH]
                                        [-g GROUP_BY]
                                        [--label-field LABEL_FIELD]
                                        [-m MIN_GENE_SIZE] [-L] [-C] [-sq]
                                        genes

Gene plot.

positional arguments:
  genes                 Genes file (GTF, BED).

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --aspect-ratio ASPECT_RATIO
                        Aspect ratio of this panel. Default is determined by
                        figure type (usually 1.0).
  --title TITLE         Title of this plot.
  --fix-chromosome      Fix chromosome identifier for this plot (add or remove
                        "chr" as required). Use this ifthere is a mismatch
                        between the nomenclature used by different datasets in
                        the figure, specifically if the chromosome prefix for
                        this dataset does not match the plot region
                        definition.
  --hide-x              Hide x-axis for this plot
  --show-minor-ticks    Show minor ticks on genome axis
  --hide-major-ticks    Hide major ticks on genome axis.
  --show-tick-legend    Show tick legend with distance between ticks on genome
                        axis
  -f FEATURE_TYPES [FEATURE_TYPES ...], --feature-types FEATURE_TYPES [FEATURE_TYPES ...]
                        Feature types to be plotted. By default only exons are
                        shown.
  -cn COLOR_NEUTRAL, --color-neutral COLOR_NEUTRAL
                        Color for genes without strand information.
  -cf COLOR_FORWARD, --color-forward COLOR_FORWARD
                        Color for genes on the '+' strand.
  -cr COLOR_REVERSE, --color-reverse COLOR_REVERSE
                        Color for genes on the '-' strand.
  -cs, --color-score    Assign color based on score value.
  -b BOX_HEIGHT, --box-height BOX_HEIGHT
                        Height of exon boxes. Default: 0.1
  -s FONT_SIZE, --font-size FONT_SIZE
                        Font size for gene labels. Default: 9
  -a ARROW_SIZE, --arrow-size ARROW_SIZE
                        Size of directionality arrows. Default: 8
  -l LINE_WIDTH, --line-width LINE_WIDTH
                        Width of the line along the length of the gene.
                        Default: 2.
  -g GROUP_BY, --group-by GROUP_BY
                        Group exons according to this attribute (e.g. for
                        plotting multiple transcripts of the same gene.
                        Default: transcript_id
  --label-field LABEL_FIELD
                        Which field to use as label.
  -m MIN_GENE_SIZE, --min-gene-size MIN_GENE_SIZE
                        If set, forces the plotted gene to be at least this
                        wide.
  -L, --no-labels       Do not plot labels on genes.
  -C, --collapse        Collapse all genes onto a single row.
  -sq, --squash         Merge all exons of each grouping unit together. Useful
                        especially when setting --group-by to "gene_id" or
                        "gene_symbol". Overlapping genes will still draw on
                        separate rows in contrast to --collapse
